Patch Precedent
===============

This project includes references to and short excerpts of relatedb/relate
(https://github.com/relatedb/relate), which is licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0, at commit 5f7a510713c3feac146133e77d8c5bb72bae1b11:

- Decision text from ADR-0585 (docs/adr/0585-installer-downloads-via-direct-route.md),
  paraphrased in evidence/installer.toml.
- Line references and check descriptions from scripts/tests/test_install_sh.sh,
  in evidence/installer.toml and in the TAP captures under tests/data/.
- Diff context from distribution/install.sh, appearing in the patches under
  fixtures/installer/.
- The subject line of the implementing commit
  5ac38808547d11f55b02333624cc3e88b46566eb, quoted in evidence/installer.toml.
- Check descriptions and line references from scripts/tests/test_release_advance.sh,
  in evidence/release.toml and in the TAP captures under tests/data/release/.
- The subject line of the implementing commit
  d79d8b150561f56b4940876a067d6b7e4781d2bc, quoted in evidence/release.toml.
- ADR titles and statuses for all decisions, quoted in
  evidence/scanned/decisions.tsv.
- File paths and line numbers of ADR citations, recorded in
  evidence/scanned/citations.tsv.
- Decision text from ADR-0580 (docs/adr/0580-post-release-workspace-versioning.md),
  paraphrased in evidence/release.toml, plus the release fixtures' diff context
  from scripts/release-bump.sh and CONTRIBUTING.md, appearing in the patches
  under fixtures/release/.
- Diff context from distribution/install.sh (the fetch_url function) in the
  token-header fixture, fixtures/installer/token-header.patch, which adds an
  Authorization header sent when GITHUB_TOKEN is set.
- The description of check #64 of scripts/tests/test_install_sh.sh ("token set:
  no Authorization header anywhere (GITHUB_TOKEN never rides a request)") and
  the line reference to lines 314-315 of that file, in evidence/installer.toml
  and in the TAP capture tests/data/token-header.tap.
- Relate CLI v1.3.0 (relate-darwin-arm64), Apache License 2.0. It is downloaded
  at run time, only when `patch-precedent fetch-relate-cli` is run, into a local
  cache after its SHA-256 is verified. It is not vendored in this repository.
- Agent transcripts under eval/results/ contain model outputs (Claude Sonnet)
  and excerpts of relatedb/relate files that the agents read, such as ADR text,
  install.sh and the test harness, at the pinned commit.

The patches in fixtures/installer/ and fixtures/release/ are authored
demonstration inputs written against Relate's code. They are not upstream
changes.

The upstream repository is fetched at run time into a local cache and is not
vendored in this repository.

Relate is copyright its authors. Apache License 2.0:
https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

Patch Precedent's own code and documentation are licensed under the MIT
License; see LICENSE. That license does not cover the Relate material
described above, which remains under Apache License 2.0.

Dependencies installed by uv are not redistributed here and keep their own
licenses. They include the `mcp` Python SDK (version 2.3.0, MIT License), used
by `patch-precedent mcp`.
relate-db 1.1.0 (Apache License 2.0) is the Python package used to read and write
the Relate store.
